      "cooked": "<p>Hi! First of all, newbie here. Played a few games so far and loved it (really hoping the UK gets more of the expansions soon). And this seems like a cool community, too.</p><p>Second, many apologies if this has been asked before...or is just a generally stupid query. I searched a fair bit, but couldn't find an answer.</p><p>One of our first games was against Citizen Dawn and Devastating Aurora came out near the start (so not too fatal, fortunately. And ultimately, we won). Now the way a couple of friends ruled it was that because it says <em>all</em> cards and nothing about 'in play', the action also destroys things in your hand as well. I had my suspicions at the time, since I couldn't really think of cards it didn't cover, but carried on anyway.</p><p>Based on what I've seen in other discussions while searching, it would appear that we made a mistake and it should only destroy things in-play and not cards you have in your hand. So, since we'll be looking to increase the difficulty in future, I want to make sure we're not handicapping ourselves unnecessarily...</p><p>Any help is much appreciated. =)</p>",
